   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The comparative",
   "texto": [
    "**-er** is added to the adjective: **schnell → schneller** (faster), **billig → billiger** (cheaper). With some short adjectives, the vocal changes: **alt → älter** (older), **groß → größer** (larger), **jung → jünger** (younger).",
    "What is compared is behind **als**: **Der Zug ist schneller als das Auto** (the train is faster than the car)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Irregular and comparative forms before the name",
   "texto": [
    "**gut → besser**, **viel → mehr**, **gern → lieber**, **hoch → höher** and **nah → näher**. **Ich fahre lieber mit dem Zug** = I prefer to go by train.",
    "The comparative can also go in front of a name and then it is declined as adjective: **ein schnellerer Zug** (a faster train), **die billigere Wohnung** (the cheapest floor). **Als** introduces what is compared to what is: **Der Zug ist schneller als der Bus**."
   ]
